{"term":"folle","lang":"fr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay_queen","concept":"gay_queen","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":44,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":87,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"French term for a flamboyant or camp gay man; literally 'madwoman'; used both as a self-identifier within gay communities and as an external mocking label.","english_term":"queen","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Feminine noun applied to gay men to emphasize campness and gender non-conformity; widely reclaimed within French gay culture; tone depends entirely on who is speaking and in what context."}
{"term":"salope","lang":"fr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"slut_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":88,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"French insult for a sexually promiscuous or morally loose woman; also a general-purpose term of abuse roughly equivalent to 'slut' or 'bitch'.","english_term":"slut","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"One of the most common French sexual insults; occupies the same cultural space as both English 'slut' (sexual connotation) and 'bitch' (general hostility); very widely used across age groups and regions."}
{"term":"pute","lang":"fr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"prostitute_slur","concept":"promiscuous_woman_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":88,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"French crude term primarily meaning prostitute; used broadly as an insult for promiscuous women and as a component of compound expletives.","english_term":"whore","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Shortened from 'putain'; primary denotation is prostitute but used far more broadly as a general insult; root of 'putain' and 'fils de pute'; ubiquitous across all French registers."}
{"term":"putain","lang":"fr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"prostitute_expletive","concept":"promiscuous_woman_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":75,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"French expletive literally meaning 'whore'; functions as an all-purpose interjection of frustration, surprise, or emphasis equivalent to 'fuck' or 'damn', and retains direct use as an insult for a promiscuous woman.","english_term":"fuck","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Etymologically means 'whore/prostitute' but in its interjection sense has drifted to a general expletive; far more socially tolerated in France than 'fuck' in Anglophone countries; appears in 'fils de pute'."}
{"term":"connard","lang":"fr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"asshole_insult","concept":"asshole_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":84,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"French masculine insult for a stupid, contemptible, or obnoxious man; derived from 'con' (etymologically from Latin 'cunnus', vagina); roughly equivalent to 'asshole' or 'dickhead'.","english_term":"asshole","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Root 'con' derives from Latin 'cunnus' (vagina) but has completely shed its anatomical meaning in modern French, functioning like English 'idiot' or 'asshole'; paired with feminine 'connasse'."}
{"term":"connasse","lang":"fr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"bitch_insult","concept":"bitch_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":87,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"French feminine insult for a stupid, contemptible, or obnoxious woman; feminine counterpart to 'connard'; roughly equivalent to 'stupid bitch'.","english_term":"stupid bitch","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Gendered counterpart to 'connard'; the gendering is grammatically obligatory in French in a way English 'asshole' is not; slightly harsher than 'connard' due to the added layer of gendered contempt."}
{"term":"fils de pute","lang":"fr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"insults","subcategory":"son_of_a_bitch","concept":"son_of_a_bitch_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":88,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"French insult literally meaning 'son of a whore'; functionally equivalent to 'son of a bitch' or 'motherfucker'; one of the most severe and widely used French insults.","english_term":"son of a bitch","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Root is 'pute' (whore) rather than 'chienne' (bitch), making the sexual etymology more explicit than the English equivalent; used both as a reactive expletive and as a deliberate severe insult; near-universal recognition."}
